          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "From there Abraham journeyed toward the territory of the Negeb, and dwelt between Kadesh and Shur; and he sojourned in Gerar. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Abraham said of Sarah his wife, “She is my sister.” And Abimelech king of Gerar sent and took Sarah. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But God came to Abimelech in a dream by night, and said to him, “Behold, you are a dead man, because of the woman whom you have taken; for she is a man's wife.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now Abimelech had not approached her; so he said, “Lord, wilt thou slay an innocent people? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Did he not himself say to me, ‘She is my sister’? And she herself said, ‘He is my brother.’ In the integrity of my heart and the innocence of my hands I have done this.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then God said to him in the dream, “Yes, I know that you have done this in the integrity of your heart, and it was I who kept you from sinning against me; therefore I did not let you touch her. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now then restore the man's wife; for he is a prophet, and he will pray for you, and you shall live. But if you do not restore her, know that you shall surely die, you, and all that are yours.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So Abimelech rose early in the morning, and called all his servants, and told them all these things; and the men were very much afraid. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Abimelech called Abraham, and said to him, “What have you done to us? And how have I sinned against you, that you have brought on me and my kingdom a great sin? You have done to me things that ought not to be done.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Abimelech said to Abraham, “What were you thinking of, that you did this thing?” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Abraham said, “I did it because I thought, There is no fear of God at all in this place, and they will kill me because of my wife. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Besides she is indeed my sister, the daughter of my father but not the daughter of my mother; and she became my wife. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when God caused me to wander from my father's house, I said to her, ‘This is the kindness you must do me: at every place to which we come, say of me, He is my brother.’ ” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Abimelech took sheep and oxen, and male and female slaves, and gave them to Abraham, and restored Sarah his wife to him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Abimelech said, “Behold, my land is before you; dwell where it pleases you.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To Sarah he said, “Behold, I have given your brother a thousand pieces of silver; it is your vindication in the eyes of all who are with you; and before every one you are righted.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Abraham prayed to God; and God healed Abimelech, and also healed his wife and female slaves so that they bore children. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 20:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " had closed all the wombs of the house of Abimelech because of Sarah, Abraham's wife.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.20.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.20.18"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
